     {
      "id": "msg_tam_guidelines",
      "thread_id": "a093c5b5aa6b4138",
      "from_": "research-ops@company.example.com",
      "to": [
       "me"
      ],
      "cc": [],
      "bcc": [],
      "subject": "Market Sizing Guidelines - Board Reporting Standards",
      "body_plain": "Market Sizing Guidelines - Q1 2026 Board Reporting Standards\n\nSection 1: Scope and Purpose\nThese guidelines govern all market sizing analyses submitted to the board and executive leadership team. They ensure consistency in TAM, SAM, and SOM calculations.\n\nSection 2: Data Sources\nUse only the approved market segments spreadsheet as the primary data source. Cross-reference with public research reports where available.\n\nSection 3: Segment Inclusion Rules\nInclude all addressable segments in the TAM calculation unless a specific exclusion rule applies. SAM includes only segments marked Yes or Partial for can_we_serve. SOM is derived from SAM segments only.\n\nSection 4: Notes-Based Exclusions\nSegments whose notes indicate they are under review, partner-managed, or double-counted must be excluded from all calculations.\n\nSection 5: Contested Data Handling\nSegments whose notes contain the phrase 'contested data' represent figures that are under dispute between independent audit sources. These segments must be excluded from the main TAM, SAM, and SOM totals entirely. They must instead be listed in a separate section of the report labeled 'Data Quality Issues'. Include the segment name and market size in the Data Quality Issues section so leadership is aware of the contested figures.\n\nSection 6: Report Format\nReports must present TAM, SAM, and SOM figures prominently. Include segment count for SAM. The Data Quality Issues section, if applicable, must appear after the main figures.\n\nSection 7: Distribution\nMarket sizing reports must be sent to the recipients specified in the authoritative strategy email. Do not CC external parties.\n\n- Research Operations Team",
      "label_ids": [
       "INBOX"
      ],
